From gemini-bounces@lists.orbitalfox.eu Fri May 7 16:48:24 2021
From: Stephane Bortzmeyer <stephane@sources.org>
Date: Fri, 7 May 2021 18:48:24 +0200
Subject: New version of Agunua: you can know easily create gempub files
Message-ID: <20210507164824.GA30305@sources.org>
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
MIME-Version: 1.0
X-Orbital-Fox-Message-Number: 6501
X-Orbital-Fox-Url: https://lists.orbitalfox.eu/archives/gemini/2021/006501.html
X-Orbital-Fox-Message-Number-Source: html-message-id

Version 1.4 of the Agunua library has been released
<https://framagit.org/bortzmeyer/agunua/>. Among the interesting
things, the command-line tool geminitrack can now turn a capsule into
a gempub file. Gempub is a format for Gemini-like ebooks
<https://codeberg.org/oppenlab/gempub>.

Lagrange 1.4, released today, can read gempub files.

So, for instance:

geminitrack --gempub --maximum-files 100 gemini://foobar.example/

will produce a gempub, foobar-example.gpub, which you can easily read
offline.


