Hi Michael,

first thing is that every gemini-site should avoid to put the user into a situation where the "back" button is the only way out, by providing arbitrary links.

And i agree with you, option "c" looks like what i would expect to see when clicking on the "back" button.

Another option is to give the end-user the choice of where back in the history to go, like if you right-click on the "back" button in the chromium browser.

Best regards from Charleston (WV),
     Frank/2

