I am sorry I misinformed you, TLS 1.2 has compression (for example
deflate), but in TLS 1.3 it has been removed. But it introduces certificate
compression to save handshake time. Although it's understandable because of
the various exploits it's unfortunate as in my opinion there are use cases,
