Hi,

First of all, introduce myself. I'm a new gemini user. I like very much the philosophy behind this.

I have a question about gemini text syntax. Is there any way to refering to link within the text? Some canonical or 

Eg. something like this:

This is my resume [1] and my work [2]

=> gemini://.... My Resumé
=> gemini://.... My work

If then I insert a link betweem "My Resumé" and "My Work", the numbers refering would be wrong.

So, is there any way to identify links within the text? Something like <a href="..." id="">.... in HTML?


Thanks in advance,
Xavier

